  "headline": "FDA lists ifosfamide shortage since 2026-06-12 with no signal at our plants",
  "headline_cites": ["E12", "D7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the ifosfamide injection shortage on 2026-06-12 and updated it through 2026-10-16, listing Baxter Healthcare, Fresenius Kabi USA LLC, Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc., and SteriMax Inc. as current.",
      "cites": ["E12", "E8", "E9", "E10", "E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "As of 2026-10-21 the shortage has been on FDA's list for 4 months.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no public FDA signal at our plants.",
      "cites": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 40 units on hand at 7.3 per day for 6 days; Corvale Lakeside has 28 units at 1.4 per day for 20 days; Corvale General has 83 units at 5.8 per day for 14 days.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked option by rule is to transfer 8 units from Corvale Lakeside to Corvale East, which would leave Lakeside with two weeks on hand and bring East to 7 days.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An approved P&T interchange allows using Hikma's 50 mg/mL concentration as an alternate to Baxter's 1 g/20 mL vial, with pharmacist verification required.",
      "cites": ["E13", "D6"]
    }
  ]
}
